      "math_academy_id": "q-182015",
      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "For the sets $X=\\{5,10\\},$ $Y=\\{r,s,t\\},$ and $Z=X\\times Y,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\nI. $(5,r)\\in Z$\n\nII. $(r,t)\\in Z$\n\nIII. $(10,s)\\in Z$",
      "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $X\\times Y$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Y.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $X\\times Y$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14123139/assets/1eb13d93fbefc4c7285edef537a9fb3e21339f7a3b37a179eeb150db8d726c1b.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(5,r),(5,s),(5,t),(10,r),(10,s),(10,t)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
